{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-103933",
  "enisaUuid": "b80c98a3-347d-3a3d-8828-398e887432e8",
  "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: accel: kxcjk-1013: reject duplicate event disable\n\nThe IIO core does not filter duplicate writes to the event enable\nattribute. kxcjk1013_write_event_config() already ignores repeated\nenable requests, but a repeated disable request still calls\nkxcjk1013_set_power_state(data, false), dropping a runtime PM reference\nthat was not acquired for this request. This can underflow the runtime\nPM usage count and trigger a \"Runtime PM usage count underflow\" warning.\n\nReturn early when the requested state already matches ev_enable_state.",
  "datePublished": "Oct 18, 2026, 3:45:38 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Oct 30, 2026, 12:38:41 PM",
  "baseScore": 0.0,
  "references": "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b33dfdc0f22dd6c9cb9ae34a32723ef0a5d2ccf5\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8c6d1abaff5dbbe2d2b7529de7f1f2395a2f07e9\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f9f88da802733bab7a87a0e685c8cfa7488f6ac\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/137c35cff4d4d69f73cbfc0bf7870bf379a7a364\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad690c0c1b9131725619e352cb7c970488cbf436\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3365209e758c845a197211645731f0e393a86012\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa94a37b5a3e560c277dac6f9e5d0d75549a6583\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd30c10ff60d2b30386c23bb7c61cc97f2385c97\n",
